<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amanirenas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 40–10 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amanirenas was a ruling queen, or kandake, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushite-empire">Kingdom of Kush</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meroe">Meroë</a>. Around 25 BCE her armies attacked Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, sacking Syene and carrying off statues of Augustus, one of whose bronze heads was buried at Meroë. After Roman counter-attacks, a peace concluded with Augustus at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samos</a> around 21 BCE remitted tribute and was favourable to Kush.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amanirenas.jpg" alt="Amanirenas" width="300" height="391" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karl Richard Lepsius (1810-84) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bar_4_Kush_queen_(Lepsius).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
